  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nA welcome pattern change remains in the offing complete with cooler \ntemps next week and daily chances for rain starting on Saturday. \nThis is all tied to a weakening upper high that drifts into East \nTexas before holding close to the Louisiana Gulf Coast for much \nof next week. This opens our door to varying degrees of monsoon \nmoisture - initially Saturday afternoon and evening and perhaps a \nmore potent version by the middle of next week. Models are in \noverall good agreement with this larger pattern, but the finer \nmesoscale details that determine precip potential and ultimately \nhow much rain falls remain unclear. This uncertainty is already a\nfactor as soon as Saturday due to a fair amount of spread in \nstorm potential accompanying the arrival of the monsoonal moisture\nplume over the Caprock. Combined with a surface trough draped SW-\nNE over the Caprock, a weak shortwave trough in southwesterly \nflow, PWATs running on average 0.5\" above normal, and ample \nheating, the pros outweigh the cons for scattered to possibly \nnumerous afternoon and evening storms. Despite these favorable \nsignals, some CAMs are curiously stingy with precip on Saturday \nwhich is not a theme shared by ensembles and global models, or \nour forecast for that matter.\n\nWeak subsidence following Saturday's shortwave could stunt \nbackground ascent for Sunday, but we'll keep a mention of PoPs \n(highest off the Caprock) as some models favor another, albeit \nweaker, upper trough or MCV drifting northeast from the Upper \nTrans-Pecos. Daily PoPs continue thereafter under an increasingly \nunsettled SW flow that turns much richer with monsoon moisture and\nperhaps some eastern Pacific tropical moisture. Whether or not a \nweak cold front sags south from the TX Panhandle on Monday remains\nto be seen, but at the very least an uptick in cloud cover and \nlower thicknesses through the week will secure cooler temperatures\nfor a change.",
